c Respiratory and Gastrointestinal Outbreaks from Free-Text Chief Complaints</article-title><source>Proceedings of the Annual Fall Symposium of the American Medical Informatics Association</source><year>2003</year><publisher-name>Madison: Omni Press</publisher-name><fpage>748</fpage><lpage>752</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Naumova</surname><given-names>EN</given-names></name><name><surname>O'Neil</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>MacNeill</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A System for Early Outbreak Detection and Signature Forecasting</article-title><source>Morbidity and Mortality Weekly Report</source><year>2005</year><volume>54</volume><fpage>77</fpage><lpage>83</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16177697</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ismail</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Pettitt</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Webster</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>'Online' monitoring and retrospective analysis of hospital outcomes based on a scan statistic</article-title><source>Statistics in Medicine</source><year>2003</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>2861</fpage><lpage>2876</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12953285</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/sim.1532</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wallenstein</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Naus</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Scan Statistics for Temporal Surveillance for Biologic Terrorism</article-title><source>Morbidity and Mortality Weekly Report</source><year>2004</year><volume>53</volume><fpage>74</fpage><lp